# Cloudflare Pages redirects and rewrites.
#
# This is the Cloudflare twin of public/_redirects plus the [[redirects]]
# blocks in netlify.toml. scripts/prepare-cloudflare.mjs copies it over
# dist/_redirects during a Cloudflare build only, so Netlify keeps using
# public/_redirects and netlify.toml untouched. When you change a rule in
# one, change it in the other.
#
# How Cloudflare differs from Netlify, and why the rules below look the way
# they do:
#   - The FIRST matching rule wins, and rules without wildcards or
#     placeholders must all come before rules with them.
#   - There is no `!` force flag. Cloudflare always applies a matching rule,
#     even when a real file exists at that path.
#   - Trailing slashes are NOT ignored when matching, so every app route
#     below also lists its trailing-slash form.
#   - HTTP -> HTTPS is not done here. Turn on "Always Use HTTPS" in the
#     Cloudflare dashboard (SSL/TLS -> Edge Certificates) instead.
#   - Unmatched paths fall through to dist/404.html, which Cloudflare serves
#     with a real 404 status. Never add a blanket `/*  /  200` here: without
#     a match Cloudflare would answer every junk URL with the homepage at 200.

# ── Retired pages -> closest live equivalent ───────────────────────────────
/services/move-in-assembly     /services/furniture-assembly   301
/services/move-in-assembly/    /services/furniture-assembly   301

# ── App routes that are deliberately NOT pre-rendered ──────────────────────
# (see ssgOptions.includedRoutes in vite.config.ts). They load the app shell
# and let the client router take over.
/admin      /   200
/admin/     /   200
/portal     /   200
/portal/    /   200
/book       /   200
/book/      /   200

/admin/*    /   200
/portal/*   /   200
/go/*       /   200
# Referral QR tokens. The uppercase rule is not redundant: the QR payload is
# uppercased to stay in QR alphanumeric mode, and paths match case-sensitively.
/r/*        /   200
/R/*        /   200
/pay/*      /   200

# ── Trailing-slash URLs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The build writes flat files (about.html, not about/index.html), and
# Cloudflare would redirect /about/ -> /about. Google flags those as "Page
# with redirect", so serve the flat page at both URLs with a 200 instead.
/:page/             /:page            200
/:section/:page/    /:section/:page   200
